  "pve": {
    "note": "Re-key the Colour adventure table on STAGE and EFFORT.\n\nThe charge was the wrong second axis. It is what the player just played,\nwhich says nothing about the Digimon, and on **DMC it does not vary at all**:\nthat module's `battle_minigame` is \"None\", which scores a flat 2 every\nbattle. So the column it played was the only column it could ever play.\n\nStage and effort are both properties of the pet, and between them they are\nwhat it has grown into and what its training bought:\n\n    stage   1-7, clamped\n    effort  0-16, drawn as four hearts at four points, so effort // 4\n\n35 rows of six rounds. `strong = round((stage - 1 + hearts) * 5 / 10)`, so\nthe two axes weigh almost evenly and the top is **five** doubles out of six,\nnever all of them -- a maxed pet still mixes its shots, which is the thing\nthat read wrong on the version this replaces.\n\n**An enemy needs no table of its own.** It has a stage and no effort at all,\nso it reads (its stage, 0 hearts) through the same door -- which is why the\nseparate `enemy_by_stage` block is gone rather than rebuilt.",
    "pattern_length": 6,
    "key": "the attacker's stage (1-7), then effort // 4 (0-4 hearts)",
